    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 3.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="282" ed="#liebermann"/>Ne synd ealle cyricean<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.17"/> na gelicre mæðe woruldlice<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.18"/> wurðscipes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.star"/> wyrðe, þeah hig godcundlice habban halsunge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.star2"/> gelice.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="282" ed="#liebermann"/>Ne synd ealle cyricean na gelicre mæðe wuruldlice weorðe, þeah hig godcundlice habban halgunge gelice.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="282" ed="#liebermann"/>quia<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.7"/> non omnes ęcclesię parem emendationis dignitatem habent<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.8"/>, licet eandem sanctificationis benedictionem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.9"/> consequantur.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.10"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="283" ed="#liebermann"/>Non enim<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.25"/> sunt omnes ęcclesię<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.26"/> unius eiusdemque<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.27"/> honoris, quamuis habeant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.28"/> unam eandemque<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.29"/> consecrationem.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="283" ed="#liebermann"/>Non enim omnes ecclesie eiusdem sunt dignitatis seculariter, licet diuinitus eandem habeant sanctificacionem.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="3a.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="156" ed="#robertson"/>Ne synd ealle cyricean na gelicre mæðe woruldlice wurðscipes<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#ICn_3-1.robnote.fn.7"/> wyrðe, þeah hig godcundlice habban hal[g]unge<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#ICn_3-1.robnote.fn.8"/> gelice.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="234" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Ne synd ealle cyricean na gelicre mæðe woruldlice wurðscipes wyrðe, þeah hig godcundlice habban halgunge gelice.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="283" ed="#liebermann"/>Keineswegs sind alle Kirchen im bürgerlichen Recht gleichen Ranges theilhaftig (ehrenwerth <hi rend="italic">G</hi>), obwohl sie kanonisch die Weihe (Gebetsbeschwörung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_3-1.lnote.de.1"/> <hi rend="italic">G</hi>) gleich haben.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Not all churches are entitled to the same rank (of honour, G) in secular terms, although they have the same consecration (exorcism, G) in ecclesiastical terms.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_3-1.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="157" ed="#robertson"/>Not all churches are to be regarded as possessing the same status in civil law, though from the side of religion they all possess the same sanctity.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="235" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Not all churches are considered alike in worldly status, although spiritually they all possess equal sanctity.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="283"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_5">VIII Atr 5</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 5</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="388"><label>from</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_5">VIII Atr 5</ref> <quote>I Cn 3:1 (from VIII Atr 5)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="388"><ref target="clause:Rect_4-4">Rect 4.4</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">G's ‘wurðscipes’ is probably G's own addition; G's ‘halsunge’ should be corrected to ‘halgunge’ from the other MSS and VIII Atr 5. Liebermann compares VIII Atr 5.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 283, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">wurðscipes: omitted A</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">halgunge: halsunge G</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-can <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-can Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wur. weorþe, <hi rend="italic">ohne</hi> wurð. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wur. weorþe, without wurð. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt übrigen Hss. und Atr.</hi> [<hi rend="italic">wohl Zusatz G's</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in the other MSS and Atr. [probably an addition of G’s]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> halgunge <hi rend="italic">aus übrigen Hss. und Atr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read halgunge from the other MSS and Atr.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quod <hi rend="italic">Hk;</hi> qui <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quod Hk; qui K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">haberet <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">haberet Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dignitatem <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dignitatem Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-quatur <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-quatur Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">283</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lb S Pl Ct Jo</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lb S Pl Ct Jo</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">283</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dei <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Dei added by Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">283</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et eiusdem <hi rend="italic">Pl Jo;</hi> et eius <hi rend="italic">Ct</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et eiusdem Pl Jo; et eius Ct</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">283</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u. h. <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u. h. Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3-1.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">283</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eandem <hi rend="italic">Di; fehlt Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eandem Di; lacking in Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_3-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">G begeht wohl einfach Schreibfehler; er meint schwerlich ‘Litanei’ bei der Weihe, ‘Auspizien’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">G probably simply makes a scribal error; he hardly means ‘litany’ at the consecration, or ‘auspices’</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_3-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">With this clause and the next, cf. VIII Atr. 5 f.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_3-1.robnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><label>wurðscipes</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_3-1.robnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><label>hal[g]unge</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">A; <hi rend="italic">halsunge</hi> G.</seg></note>
      </div>
